{
  "fixture": "group-calculations",
  "version": 1,
  "encoding": {
    "supported_field_types": "FieldType ints that offer a board group calculation (WP09 §1.6).",
    "valid_types_by_field_type": "CalculationType ints valid for each supported field type, in menu order (desktop calculationsForFieldType without Count, which is Count all, and CountValue).",
    "calculation_to_aggregation": "The R-FORMAT aggregation (formatChartValue ctx.aggregation) of each CalculationType.",
    "field": "type is a FieldType int; number_format a NumberFormat id; date_format a DateFormat id; options [id, name] pairs.",
    "cells": "One cell per row, in row order. Text and URL: the text. Number: a number (stored as its JS String()) or a raw string. Select: an option id or a list of option ids ([] is an empty selection). Checkbox: true or false. Checklist: {tasks: [[name, done]]}. DateTime: a timestamp in seconds. null: the row has no cell. CreatedTime and LastEditedTime come from row_timestamps (seconds), never from cells.",
    "computation": "The column's rows go through the desktop CalculationsService (calculate_with_numeric) with the cell rules of calculate_rows_while_open: CreatedTime and LastEditedTime from the row timestamps, a missing checkbox counts as unchecked, and total_row_count is the number of rows. Web computeBoardGroupCalculation must reproduce expected exactly (numbers within 1e-9).",
    "expected": "{kind: none} | {kind: number, value} | {kind: date, timestamp_ms}. The raw number of the service becomes number; DateEarliest and DateLatest become date; DateRange becomes number of days ((latest - earliest) / 86400, from two or more dates); an aggregation without a value (a numeric one over zero numbers, a percent over zero rows) is none. Generated by the ignored Rust test regenerate_group_calculation_vectors.",
    "formatted": "formatChartValue(value, {aggregation: calculation_to_aggregation[type], yField, mode: tooltip, locale: en-US, timeZone}) where yField is {type: number, numberFormat}, {type: date, dateFormat}, {type: checkbox} or {type: other} by field, a date value is timestamp_ms / 86400000 days and time_zone is the case's (every date case is UTC). none formats as \"\"."
  },
